WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:14.786
The next day was Sunday, and Dr.

2
00:00:14.866 --> 00:00:17.508
Firth came to examine Dan's injured foot.

3
00:00:17.528 --> 00:00:23.573
"You must keep Dan quiet for at least a week," Dr.

4
00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:24.734
Firth said to Jo.

5
00:00:24.754 --> 00:00:28.757
"After that he may be able to walk with a crutch."

6
00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:31.760
"I will get better, right?"

7
00:00:32.076 --> 00:00:33.336
Dan asked anxiously.

8
00:00:33.356 --> 00:00:36.437
"I hope so," Dr.

9
00:00:36.477 --> 00:00:39.898
Firth said, returning his instruments to his black bag.

10
00:00:39.918 --> 00:00:45.620
"But remember, absolutely no walking or standing on that foot!"

11
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.121
After the doctor left, Dan shifted uncomfortably in bed.

12
00:00:51.141 --> 00:00:54.962
"What if my foot is like this forever?"

13
00:00:55.362 --> 00:00:56.163
he asked Jo.

14
00:00:56.183 --> 00:01:01.324
"I'm famous for my nursing skills, and I won't let that happen."

15
00:01:01.804 --> 00:01:07.546
Jo tried to sound reassuring, though she wasn't confident he'd recover completely.

16
00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:11.807
"Now, would you like some of the boys to visit?"

17
00:01:11.827 --> 00:01:19.669
"Yes, please, Nat and Demi, and I'd like my bundle too, if you haven't thrown it away."

18
00:01:21.049 --> 00:01:23.430
An anxious look crossed Dan's face again.

19
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:30.432
"I kept it because I could tell it contained something special," Jo said.

20
00:01:31.004 --> 00:01:35.165
She left the room and soon returned with Dan's bundle and the boys.

21
00:01:35.185 --> 00:01:37.366
"Dan, you're back!"

22
00:01:37.826 --> 00:01:40.347
Nat said, pleased to see his old friend.

23
00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:43.547
"Whoa! Look at those!"

24
00:01:44.028 --> 00:01:48.409
Demi said as Dan unpacked birds' eggs wrapped in moss.

25
00:01:49.749 --> 00:01:53.110
Three black beetles crawled from underneath a smooth stone.

26
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.611
"How did you find all this stuff?"

27
00:01:56.631 --> 00:02:00.632
"Well, you have to know where to look," Dan said.

28
00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:09.238
"When you turn this stone over Jo smiled to herself as she slipped away.

29
00:02:09.258 --> 00:02:17.260
"If Dan grows up to be a naturalist and Nat becomes a musician, then I'll have done an

30
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.061
excellent job with these two."

31
00:02:20.981 --> 00:02:26.603
Dan's admirers were so fascinated by his stories that they almost missed their Sunday walk.

32
00:02:28.903 --> 00:02:29.384
When Mr.

33
00:02:29.424 --> 00:02:32.681
Bauer came to fetch them, Dan looked disappointed.

34
00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:37.583
"Let's move you into the parlor for a change of scenery."

35
00:02:38.763 --> 00:02:42.725
The professor gently picked up Dan, who tried to smile.

36
00:02:45.447 --> 00:02:50.089
After everyone had left, Jo came into the parlor with Teddy and Rob.

37
00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:54.611
"You're a city boy," she said to Dan.

38
00:02:54.631 --> 00:02:57.332
"How did you get interested in nature?"

39
00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.022
"I didn't know much until I met Mr.

40
00:03:01.082 --> 00:03:03.784
Hyde—a naturalist who used to stay at Mr.

41
00:03:03.824 --> 00:03:09.088
Page's. Sometimes he'd ask me to assist him with his observations.

42
00:03:10.409 --> 00:03:12.611
Mr. Page thought it was silly, but Mr.

43
00:03:12.671 --> 00:03:15.493
Hyde could lie still for hours watching a bird.

44
00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.676
He knew so much about everything!"

45
00:03:20.137 --> 00:03:21.498
Dan paused for breath.

46
00:03:21.518 --> 00:03:25.041
"I hope I'll get to see him again sometime."

47
00:03:25.061 --> 00:03:30.945
"I hope so too," Jo said, noticing how cheerful Dan had become.

48
00:03:30.965 --> 00:03:36.849
"If you really love those things, I'll make sure you have time to study them."

49
00:03:38.169 --> 00:03:42.952
Dan broke into a wide grin, but his face fell at Jo's next announcement.

50
00:03:42.972 --> 00:03:48.715
"However, you must also work on improving your behavior," she added firmly.

51
00:03:50.436 --> 00:03:52.437
Dan pointed to his injured foot.

52
00:03:52.457 --> 00:03:57.620
"How can I possibly do that when I can't even go anywhere?"

53
00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:05.103
"You can be patient and cheerful despite your pain, and you can help me," Jo said.

54
00:04:05.123 --> 00:04:12.486
"You can amuse Rob and Teddy, or wind yarn into balls, or read to me while I sew."

55
00:04:12.506 --> 00:04:16.708
"Yes, ma'am, I'll try to—" "Dan!

56
00:04:17.028 --> 00:04:18.489
Look what I found for you!"

57
00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:24.112
Just then Demi raced into the parlor with a toad in each hand.

58
00:04:26.456 --> 00:04:27.457
"I don't think Mrs.

59
00:04:27.537 --> 00:04:29.819
Bauer will let me keep those toads in the house."

60
00:04:30.799 --> 00:04:33.001
Dan looked hesitantly at Jo.

61
00:04:33.021 --> 00:04:35.163
"Will you?"

62
00:04:38.405 --> 00:04:40.867
Jo laughed and shook her head no.

63
00:04:40.887 --> 00:04:47.192
"If you tell me what to do, I'll take care of them in the barn," Demi offered.

64
00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:52.916
So Dan gave him some instructions, and Demi carried the creatures away.

65
00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:59.991
"Demi cut short his walk to bring me those toads," Dan said, sounding amazed.

66
00:05:00.011 --> 00:05:03.253
"He must have learned how to be nice at home.

67
00:05:03.273 --> 00:05:06.014
He's lucky to have parents to help him."

68
00:05:07.335 --> 00:05:11.497
"Yes, my sister Meg and her husband, John, are very kind people.

69
00:05:12.798 --> 00:05:17.401
They've been a good influence on Demi," Jo said, and patted Dan's shoulder.

70
00:05:17.421 --> 00:05:21.623
"And now you have all of us to help you."

71
00:05:23.788 --> 00:05:27.869
Dan spent the next week resting, and on Saturday Dr.

72
00:05:27.949 --> 00:05:30.650
Firth declared him well enough to use a crutch.

73
00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:34.911
"Hooray!" Nat rushed off to tell the others.

74
00:05:36.892 --> 00:05:41.213
After lunch Dan limped onto the front porch and sat in a rocker.

75
00:05:42.974 --> 00:05:46.615
Everyone gathered around him to talk and play quiet games.

76
00:05:46.635 --> 00:05:50.456
"Uncle Laurie's here!"

77
00:05:50.928 --> 00:05:54.069
Rob suddenly shouted as a carriage came up the drive.

78
00:05:56.030 --> 00:06:00.792
When the carriage stopped in front of the house, Laurie emerged with his daughter, Bess.

79
00:06:02.273 --> 00:06:08.095
Daisy took Bess to her kitchen, and some of the others disappeared to check the gardens and animals.

80
00:06:09.516 --> 00:06:13.217
They wanted everything to look nice for Laurie's inspection.

81
00:06:13.237 --> 00:06:17.979
"I bet you're tired of staying in the house," Laurie said to Dan.

82
00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.140
"Oh, yes!"

83
00:06:20.608 --> 00:06:22.089
Dan blurted out quickly.

84
00:06:22.109 --> 00:06:26.351
"Then let's take Dan for a drive," Laurie said to Nat.

85
00:06:26.371 --> 00:06:28.333
"Go fetch a cushion."

86
00:06:30.674 --> 00:06:35.477
Dan was soon settled in the carriage, his foot resting comfortably upon a cushion.

87
00:06:35.497 --> 00:06:38.819
"I have a book here that you might like."

88
00:06:39.219 --> 00:06:40.800
Laurie reached under the seat.

89
00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:45.102
"Mrs. Bauer told me you're interested in nature."

90
00:06:45.122 --> 00:06:54.813
"Wow!" Dan exclaimed as he studied the colorful pictures of birds, butterflies, and other insects.

91
00:06:56.935 --> 00:07:00.558
Nat leaned over Dan's shoulder for a glimpse of the illustrations.

92
00:07:02.079 --> 00:07:02.840
"You know, Mrs.

93
00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.362
Bauer is very nice," Laurie said.

94
00:07:05.382 --> 00:07:10.286
"But you can't expect her to put up with every creature and nest you boys bring into the

95
00:07:10.326 --> 00:07:17.092
house. This school needs a natural history museum, and I think Dan should be the curator."

96
00:07:20.288 --> 00:07:23.992
Dan hugged the book to his chest with a delighted smile.

97
00:07:24.012 --> 00:07:27.976
"Thank you, sir—that sounds wonderful."
